From: Alex Richardson <Alexander.Richardson@cl.cam.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 12 Mar 2021 11:15:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] compiler-rt: Backport the ARM inexact status-bit correction

Adapt upstream LLVM e2cd2f7d08ce4391f19c0ce5c4ea63bb9a985fcf
([builtins] Fix value of ARM_INEXACT) to the active Android 11.0.2
r383902b1 ARM builtins prebuilt.

ARM_INEXACT must set FPSCR IXC (0x10), not IXE (0x1000). The old
value turns an ordinary inexact __aeabi_fadd result into an enabled
VFP trap. MiOne's legacy eCompass subsequently dies with SIGFPE
FPE_FLTRES in sqrtf, taking down SensorService and system_server.

Keep the existing archive and replace only the ORR immediate in
fp_mode.c.o's .text.__fe_raise_inexact: ORR r0,r0,#4096 becomes
ORR r0,r0,#16. Exactly two bytes change at archive offsets 5764/5765;
archive size, symbols, index, and every other object are unchanged.
No blanket floating-point exception suppression is added.

Before SHA256: c78d0076fb86e3a7428649cb1b611251373f4e572b67ef8f6956ad59b2cf40ea
After SHA256: 611ca36071ee503d03363425703c7d3a2184a92c2edf6d92706144aaf5a9d6d9
Upstream: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/e2cd2f7d08ce4391f19c0ce5c4ea63bb9a985fcf
Reviewed upstream by: kongyi, peter.smith
Differential Revision: https://reviews.llvm.org/D98353

Test: bounded Android build; disassemble the resulting runtime/bootstrap
libc; run the legacy sensor HAL on MiOne with the screen on. Magnetic,
orientation and geomagnetic samples arrive; no SIGFPE, SensorService
abort or system_server replacement. Wi-Fi scans with the original MAC.

